WEBVTT

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:26.730
Let's get going now please.

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:36.990
You don't need to be so anxious.

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:38.840
I'll have you back soon.

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:44.580
I want you to give me what you inherited from him.

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:49.540
He's going to cause a terrible calamity.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:54.900
If you could give me your cooperation, we can stop that from happening.

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:59.000
I don't believe that.

00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:03.810
That's fine.  I have something I'd like you to see.

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:08.560
It will help you learn who he truly is.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:20.320
Young lady, it's almost time for dinner.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:31.830
Young lady!

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:44.850
There he is.

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:48.310
Chiko!

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:08.620
Where's that old man planning to take Chiko?

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:46.780
Which way did they go?

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:17.710
Damn it!  Without my bike, I'll never catch up to Chiko.

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:28.600
She's a monster.

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:41.050
I've found you.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:46.130
I knew it.  You've got reinforced muscles.

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:08.160
How ugly.

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:11.370
Take this!

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:44.070
She had a beautiful body with no side effects.

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:47.630
And her emotions were completely repressed.

00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:50.380
Hey, what was that?

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:52.580
Do you know the old man in the car?

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:55.950
He took a girl I know with him.

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:58.100
Mikamo Chizuko...

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:00.330
The Daughter of Twenty Faces, right?

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:02.030
You know about Chiko...

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:04.470
Who are you?

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:27.310
The sound of water?

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:42.590
There's a system of underground waterways laid out beneath Tokyo that I suppose you might call a parting gift from the war.

00:06:42.590 --> 00:06:45.420
You see, water was essential for my research.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:52.300
Chizuko-san, did you know that besides liquid, gas, and solid,

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:55.390
water can take on a fourth form?

00:06:57.870 --> 00:07:02.400
But imagine if there was a fourth form that no one knew about.

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:05.440
Twenty Faces said the same thing.

00:07:06.010 --> 00:07:11.150
We refer to it as the fourth state of water.

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:16.900
I heard that Twenty Faces was involved with the fourth state of water.

00:07:18.010 --> 00:07:24.420
The fourth state of water is produced when you apply extreme heat and pressure to water.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:26.880
It's a compressed mass of vast energy.

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:30.390
When it happens, it's like witnessing a miracle.

00:07:30.390 --> 00:07:32.910
Water turns into light.

00:07:33.510 --> 00:07:34.280
Light?

00:07:34.570 --> 00:07:36.970
Turn water into light...

00:07:37.090 --> 00:07:38.940
It's all connected.

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:42.980
That poem by Éluard is what I inherited from him.

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:54.100
Come.

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:11.300
But he took the research for himself and broke away from me.

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:17.030
And if that wasn't bad enough, he's plotting to cause a great disaster using the fourth state of water.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:21.840
In order to stop him I must be allowed to finish my research,

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:24.630
even if I have to do it all by myself.

00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:54.820
What's going on, Akechi-san?  I wasn't expecting you.

00:08:55.460 --> 00:08:57.580
I'm very busy.

00:08:57.580 --> 00:08:59.620
Kawada-san, I have something important to discuss.

00:09:00.590 --> 00:09:02.930
Do you know a man named Kakishima Kouhei?

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:05.850
Hmm, I guess not.

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:13.050
During the war, he was a researcher who was involved in weapons development for the military.

00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:18.340
It appears that man is going to attempt a very dangerous experiment underneath Tokyo.

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:22.890
What, now?  The war's over, you know.

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:27.050
In that case, what if I said that Kakishima was connected to Twenty Faces?

00:09:27.050 --> 00:09:27.650
What?

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:32.750
Kakishima disappeared from normal society shortly after the war ended.

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:37.060
Around that exact time, the phantom thief Twenty Faces appeared.

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:38.850
But that's not really...

00:09:38.850 --> 00:09:39.530
There's more.

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:44.990
A man who worked in his research lab was murdered in Toran, England.

00:09:44.990 --> 00:09:48.040
Immediately afterwards, Twenty Faces was spotted in Toran.

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:50.800
Are these just coincidences?

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:56.200
There's some sort of connection between Kakishima and Twenty Faces.

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:58.680
They may even be the same person.

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:00.450
What?

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:02.210
Kakishima is dangerous.

00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:05.090
He spent the days of the war together with the military.

00:10:05.090 --> 00:10:06.930
We can't wait until after he acts!

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:11.420
We haven't a moment to spare.

00:10:13.430 --> 00:10:15.420
It's my fault.

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:21.050
I scolded her, telling her to stop thinking about Twenty Faces.

00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:24.030
It'll be fine, Tome-kun.

00:10:24.030 --> 00:10:26.470
Chizuko-kun is a level-headed girl.

00:10:26.470 --> 00:10:29.500
She knows what she should do.

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:32.960
But, she's just a normal girl.

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:38.570
No matter what fate may have in store for her, she's still just a thirteen-year-old child.

00:10:39.170 --> 00:10:41.760
That's why I'm so worried.

00:10:45.640 --> 00:10:47.230
I couldn't agree more.

00:10:47.230 --> 00:10:50.530
So we adults must stay strong, right?

00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:56.240
OK!  How about the two of us go in search of Chizuko-kun?

00:10:56.240 --> 00:10:57.340
Yes.

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:02.960
How about it?

00:11:03.940 --> 00:11:05.980
Why did you bring me here?

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:07.980
I wanted you to see it.

00:11:08.920 --> 00:11:12.100
The research he and I sacrificed everything for.

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:41.660
Watch closely.

00:11:51.430 --> 00:11:55.900
Oscillation waves from the three towers will awaken a reaction in the water.

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:59.940
And that will give birth to the fourth state of water.

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:20.190
It's pretty.

00:12:20.190 --> 00:12:23.010
Heh, it may appear beautiful,

00:12:23.690 --> 00:12:27.730
but this amount of light isn't even close to the fourth state.

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:35.810
The oscillation waves aren't tuned to the exact parameters.

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:39.270
The cause of that is its natural resonance.

00:12:39.950 --> 00:12:42.810
In order to make water reach the fourth state,

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:47.030
you need to input the exact parameters so as to cancel out that resonance.

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:54.290
He discovered them and left with the values of all three parameters.

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:56.330
And I believe you know them.

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:58.740
Three parameters?

00:12:58.740 --> 00:13:01.640
Could they have been in that Éluard poem he sang to me?

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:05.070
Resonance?

00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:26.920
I knew it.  He left all of it behind...

00:13:26.920 --> 00:13:29.410
...somewhere inside this girl.

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:37.210
Why?!  Why did you tie us to the military without consulting me?

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:41.670
F-For your sake, I...

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:44.440
...I've become a murderer.

00:13:45.360 --> 00:13:47.300
Why?

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:49.170
Why isn't it working?

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:51.100
What am I missing?!

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:57.850
Why?

00:13:57.850 --> 00:14:00.560
We need to cancel out its natural resonance.

00:14:06.590 --> 00:14:08.450
Did you see the light?

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:11.970
It was a beautiful light.

00:14:12.890 --> 00:14:14.830
Much too much for us to handle.

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:22.820
I intend to seal away all my research.

00:14:43.130 --> 00:14:44.900
It's as you see.

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:48.230
If he hadn't betrayed me...

00:14:48.230 --> 00:14:50.910
If he didn't take the research for himself...

00:14:50.910 --> 00:14:53.970
I would have obtained the light!

00:14:53.970 --> 00:14:57.560
And to entrust it to a girl who doesn't know anything!

00:15:03.320 --> 00:15:07.850
Come now!  Please give me what you inherited from him.

00:15:10.140 --> 00:15:11.890
You still don't get it?

00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:15.160
He didn't just betray me.

00:15:15.160 --> 00:15:17.890
He's trying to betray you too!

00:15:18.590 --> 00:15:21.530
The man who you trusted from the bottom of your heart...

00:15:21.530 --> 00:15:24.430
...is trying to take away your future!

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:28.900
He's not like that.

00:15:29.750 --> 00:15:31.640
How do you know that?

00:15:31.640 --> 00:15:33.940
You're just one of his pawns.

00:15:33.940 --> 00:15:36.330
You don't know a single thing about him.

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:38.240
I do know!

00:15:38.240 --> 00:15:42.540
I learned it during the two years I spent with him.

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:47.150
He rescued me from despair.

00:15:47.770 --> 00:15:52.630
And then he gave me a new family and times that were irreplaceable.

00:15:53.390 --> 00:15:57.850
He found the light that lives within me!

00:15:58.970 --> 00:16:03.040
He even told me about the fourth form of water.

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:06.030
It's pretty, isn't it?

00:16:06.030 --> 00:16:09.940
Beautiful things enrich the heart.

00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:13.340
He smiled.

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:18.460
He didn't perform his research just as a scientist!

00:16:19.530 --> 00:16:23.340
He wanted to see that unbelievably beautiful form of water!

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:27.540
But you never picked up on that feeling!

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:32.220
You're not like him.

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:36.390
I will not give you what I received from him!

00:16:43.960 --> 00:16:45.700
I see.

00:16:45.700 --> 00:16:48.110
So you've chosen him as well?

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:54.250
Then I have no choice.

00:17:04.450 --> 00:17:05.330
It's you!

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:29.220
Koito-san!

00:17:29.220 --> 00:17:32.670
You said you'd always protect her, didn't you?

00:17:33.650 --> 00:17:38.160
I plan to find out what's really important to you.

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:45.520
Stop!

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:49.290
You are aware that the human body contains water, are you not?

00:17:50.260 --> 00:17:53.300
So I'm going to use her for an experiment.

00:18:10.330 --> 00:18:11.600
Fine.

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:17.210
Mister...

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:22.330
Chiko, you can hear songs here too.

00:18:23.220 --> 00:18:25.720
The sound of the grass, wind, and sky...

00:18:25.720 --> 00:18:29.350
Their natural resonances play a spectacular melody.

00:18:30.160 --> 00:18:31.860
The resonance is a song?

00:18:32.740 --> 00:18:34.340
Yes, exactly.

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:40.340
It is the warm law of men

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:45.370
From grapes, they make the wine

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:49.370
From coals, they make the fire

00:18:50.140 --> 00:18:53.860
From kisses, they make the men

00:18:55.620 --> 00:18:58.860
It is the warm law...

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:01.870
...of men

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:05.870
From grapes, they make the wine

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:10.640
From coals, they make the fire

00:19:10.640 --> 00:19:15.240
From kisses, they make the men

00:19:15.240 --> 00:19:17.960
That's the song I heard on that hill.

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:20.900
He taught me that song.

00:19:21.780 --> 00:19:24.740
Just as water is changed into light,

00:19:24.740 --> 00:19:28.500
there are three transformations within Éluard's poem.

00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:30.400
Grapes to wine.

00:19:30.400 --> 00:19:32.110
Coal to fire.

00:19:32.110 --> 00:19:33.900
Kisses to men.

00:19:36.330 --> 00:19:39.150
If you use the difference in the musical pitch of each word...

00:19:39.150 --> 00:19:41.520
...as the parameters...

00:19:41.520 --> 00:19:43.230
I see.

00:19:43.230 --> 00:19:45.980
He hid the three parameters in a song.

00:19:47.020 --> 00:19:49.160
That's something he'd think of doing.

00:19:50.610 --> 00:19:52.570
Thank you, Chizuko-kun.

00:19:52.570 --> 00:19:55.840
Thanks to you, I can complete the research now.

00:20:04.720 --> 00:20:05.450
Stop!

00:20:20.990 --> 00:20:23.200
Sorry to keep you waiting, Chiko.

00:20:24.760 --> 00:20:25.570
Mister?

00:20:42.980 --> 00:20:44.340
Mister.

00:20:51.220 --> 00:20:53.750
D-Damn you!

00:20:54.540 --> 00:20:56.940
Let's settle this once and for all,

00:20:56.940 --> 00:20:57.980
Professor.
